# Monitor layout for this machine. Managed by hyprmon, NOT tracked in git.
#
# install.sh seeds this file from monitors.conf.example when it is missing.
# hyprmon (via the ~/.config/bin/hyprmon wrapper) owns everything below and
# rewrites it on every profile apply -- don't hand-edit it expecting the change
# to survive, and don't commit it.
#
# hyprland.conf sources this file last, after machines/$HOST.conf, so whatever
# hyprmon writes here wins over the per-host defaults.
#
# Per-host settings that SHOULD be tracked (GDK_SCALE, lid bindings, and the
# fixed layout of a desktop that never changes) belong in machines/$HOST.conf.
#
# Deliberately no `monitor =` lines here: hyprmon replaces the first run of
# monitor lines it finds and appends them at the end when it finds none, so an
# empty file is a clean slate. Without any monitor rule at all, Hyprland falls
# back to its own `preferred, auto, 1` default, which is a sane starting point.
